  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 217 AM EDT Sat Apr 18 2026\n\nUnfortunately, little hope for wetter weather is in the immediate \noffing in the wake of our weekend cold front. High pressure will \nbuild in at the surface amid initial northwest flow aloft ushering \nin much drier and more temperate conditions early next week. This \nmuch drier airmass will lead to persistent fire weather concerns \ngiven ongoing drought conditions and limited rainfall with the \nweekend system. Very low relative humidity values each day will lead \nto Fire Danger conditions at a minimum with some potential for Red \nFlag concerns, especially early week (Monday) time frame with higher \nforecast winds. \n\nAfter the brief early week cooldown, temperatures will quickly warm \nback above normal by mid to late week as upper ridging expands back \neastward. Any promising chance for beneficial rainfall will hold off \nuntil at least next weekend when a more favorable pattern for \nrainfall could perhaps return. As such, rainfall deficits will \ncontinue to mount.",
